+To assess whether the final-year Sharpe--complexity profile is representative
+of the broader historical record, Figure~\ref{fig:complexity_nine} repeats
+the analysis across nine nonoverlapping investment periods. Holding the
+Gaussian representation fixed, we vary only the degree of regularization
+and evaluate each candidate on subsequent portfolio returns. The profiles
+show that realized performance need not improve monotonically as additional
+portfolio directions are activated. In several periods, Sharpe reaches an
+interior maximum and subsequently declines, although the magnitude of the
